# deploy/research.Dockerfile's own ignore file. Docker looks for
# <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile and, when present,
# uses it INSTEAD of the repository's own .dockerignore for that build --
# so this file, not the top-level one (whose *.md/!README.md pair and other
# rules are the engine image's concerns), is what actually governs what
# reaches ohcamel-research's image.
#
# research.Dockerfile copies exactly four repo-relative trees: research/,
# interface/, fixtures/macro/ and fixtures/history/. Everything below either
# trims what those COPYs pull in, or drops trees none of them ever touch (kept
# out mainly to keep the build context this Dockerfile sends to the daemon
# small; no COPY here could reach them regardless).
#
# How a pattern matches: against the whole path from the context root, and
# `*` never crosses a `/`. A bare `.env` or `*.pyc` therefore matches at the
# root only -- research/.env or research/src/.../x.pyc would slip through it.
# `**/` matches any number of directories, none included, so every pattern
# that must hold at any depth below starts with it.

# Never baked into any image, at any depth: an image layer is permanent, and
# live mode's secrets reach the container through an env_file mount at
# runtime, never a COPY (see docker-compose.yml's ohcamel-research entry).
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env

# Local, regenerated, or otherwise dev-only files and trees, at any depth.
research/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Uncommitted battery run artifacts. research/experiments/ is otherwise
# copied whole, so its manifest.*.json files and each experiment's
# config.yaml -- both required for the staleness check below to run at all --
# reach the image with no pattern of their own.
research/experiments/*/results/

# Markdown at the context root only (see "How a pattern matches" above):
# README.md, CLAUDE.md and the like. Nothing inside the four copied trees
# is touched by it -- research/README.md, research/experiments/*/
# hypothesis.md and report.md, interface/README.md and
# fixtures/history/README.md all reach the image. Only research/README.md
# is read there (research/pyproject.toml's `readme = "README.md"` makes
# hatchling refuse to build the project without it, in `uv sync --locked`);
# the rest are inert, and none is hashed into a manifest. The re-include
# changes nothing today; it is here so that widening `*.md` to `**/*.md`
# could never drop the one markdown file the build needs.
*.md
!research/README.md

# Everything the staleness check (research.Dockerfile's is_stale RUN step)
# hashes must reach the image: battery/'s files (never its __pycache__ or
# *.pyc, which is_stale does not hash either), each experiment's
# config.yaml, research/config/friction_v1.yaml, research/uv.lock, and
# fixtures/history/ and fixtures/macro/'s parquet files and .meta.json
# sidecars. No exclusion above matches any of them, so none needs a
# re-include -- and one for battery/** would, coming later, re-include the
# *.pyc and __pycache__/ excluded above. The manifests themselves are named
# outright, as before, so this file says they reach the image rather than
# leaving it to omission.
!research/experiments/*/manifest.*.json

# Everything outside the four trees research.Dockerfile actually copies.
desk/
lib/
web/
bin/
test/
bench/
docs/
deploy/
.git/
.github/
.superpowers/
_build/
_opam/
_coverage/
book.sexp
book.example.sexp
desk.db*
Untitled
notes.txt
claudecodehandoff.md
*.pdf
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
